MCSKIP MT,<>
MCINS %.
A closing delimiter can be left outside the construction it closes,
so that one newline can close a call and then close the call that
contains it. The node flag zero says so.
MCDEF ADD , NL N0 AS <(add %A1. to %A2.)>
MCDEF IF THEN NL AS <[if %A1. then %A2.]>
ADD x,y
IF ready THEN ADD p,q
